## PHASE 2 — The Pocket Adventure Engine (Week 3–6)
### Goal: Build the actual thing people will use.

### 2.1 Platform decision

> **Not a native app. Not yet.**

Build a **Progressive Web App (PWA)**.

Why:
- No App Store review process (Apple would take weeks)
- Works on every phone immediately
- Can be "installed" to home screen
- Push notifications work (on Android, limited on iOS but improving)
- You can ship daily without waiting for approvals
- Feels native enough for what we need

**Tech stack:**
```
Framework:    Next.js (App Router) or SvelteKit
Styling:      Keep the scrapbook CSS system we already built
Auth:         Supabase Auth (magic link — no passwords, matches the vibe)
Database:     Supabase (Postgres)
Real-time:    Supabase Realtime (for live features later)
Storage:      Supabase Storage (photos, drawings)
Hosting:      Vercel
PWA:          next-pwa or vite-plugin-pwa
```

### 2.2 Core screens

#### Home — "Today's Mission"
- Shows one (or up to three) Pocket Adventures for today
- Each adventure has:
  - The mission prompt
  - A visual object (fortune cookie, folded note, etc. — reuse our system)
  - "Do it solo" or "Find a sidekick" buttons
  - An estimated vibe: 🧸 cozy / 🎪 chaotic / 🔬 weird

#### Solo mode
- Do the mission alone
- Upload a result: photo, drawing, text, voice note
- Gets added to your personal "Pocket Museum" (collection of past missions)
- Can be shared as a card to Instagram/WhatsApp

#### Sidekick mode (the social magic)
- "Find someone nearby who also wants to do this"
- Location-based matching (not profile-based, not interest-based)
- **No profiles. No bios. No photos.** Just: "this person is 0.5km away and also wants to find the ugliest rock"
- You both accept → you get each other's first name and a meeting point suggestion
- After the mission: both rate the experience (not each other — the EXPERIENCE)
  - "Was it funny?" "Would you do another mission with this person?"

#### Pocket Museum
- Your personal collection of completed missions
- Each entry: the mission, your result, the date, who you did it with
- Looks like a scrapbook page. Not a feed. Not a grid. A scrapbook.
- Optional: mark someone as a "recurring sidekick" (this is how friendships form)

### 2.3 The mission engine
- Missions are **curated, not user-generated** (at first)
- We write 100+ missions across categories:
  - 🪨 Object quests (find/make/bring something)
  - 🎨 Creative challenges (draw/build/invent)
  - 🗣️ Conversation starters (questions/debates/stories)
  - 🏃 Outdoor adventures (explore/walk/discover)
  - 🤝 Partner missions (require 2+ people)
- Each mission has metadata:
  - Solo-able? Group-able? Indoor/outdoor? Time required?
  - Weather-appropriate? (don't suggest "find the best puddle" on a sunny day)
- Missions rotate. Some are daily, some weekly, some seasonal.
- **Special missions** for holidays, weather events, local festivals

