## PHASE 3 — Community & Retention (Week 7–10)
### Goal: Keep people coming back. Build real connections.

### 3.1 Sidekick Streaks
- Not gamification in the Duolingo sense
- More like: "You've done 5 missions this month. Here's a tiny badge."
- Badges are silly: "Rock Enthusiast" "Professional Nonsense-er" "Leaf Ranker"
- They show up in your Pocket Museum

### 3.2 City boards
- Each unlocked city gets a "bulletin board" (like the one on our landing page)
- People can pin completed missions, funny results, photos
- Moderated but not sanitised. Keep the weird energy.
- This is where community forms

### 3.3 Recurring Sidekicks
- If you and someone do 3+ missions together, the app suggests:
  > "You and Maya have done 3 missions together. Want to make it official?"
- "Official" just means you can directly invite each other to future missions
- This is the natural friendship formation path

### 3.4 Group missions
- Some missions are designed for 3-6 people
- "Build the ugliest birthday card" needs a group
- Groups form organically: recurring sidekicks invite each other
- No "create a group" button. Just: "Invite your sidekicks to this mission"

### 3.5 The Dispatch evolves
- Weekly email becomes more personal:
  - "You did 2 missions this week. 847 people in London did them too."
  - "Most popular result from Rock Olympics this week: [photo]"
  - "New mission dropping Friday. It involves potatoes."

