## PHASE 4 — The Physical Layer (Week 11–16)
### Goal: Bridge digital and physical. This is where Sidekick becomes REAL.

### 4.1 Sidekick Kits
- Physical boxes mailed to members:
  - 4 crayons (specific colours we choose)
  - A tiny notebook
  - A sticker sheet (our doodle aesthetic)
  - 5 printed mission cards
  - A smooth rock (yes, actually)
- These become the objects people USE during missions
- Cost: ~$8 to produce, sell at $15 or give free to top community members

### 4.2 Pop-up Sidekick Sessions
- In unlocked cities, organise real meetups
- Not "networking events." Not "happy hours."
- "Show up at this park on Saturday at 3pm. Bring one crayon."
- We provide the missions. People provide the nonsense.
- Document everything. Photos, videos, stories → back to the app

### 4.3 Partner locations
- Cafes, bookshops, parks that become "Sidekick spots"
- They get a little sign: "Sidekick missions available here"
- Maybe a jar of mission cards on the counter
- In exchange: we drive foot traffic, they give us a community space

