## PHASE 5 — Monetisation (Week 16+)
### Goal: Make money without ruining the vibe.

> Rule: if it feels corporate, we don't do it.

### 5.1 Sidekick Membership — $3/month or $25/year
What you get:
- Access to "premium" missions (more elaborate, multi-day, seasonal)
- Pocket Museum customisation (different scrapbook styles)
- Early access to Sidekick Kits
- Your name hand-written (digitally) in the credits page
- A real sticker mailed to you once

### 5.2 Sidekick Kits (physical product)
- Sell kits as one-time purchases
- Seasonal editions: Summer Kit, Rainy Day Kit, Holiday Kit
- Gift-able: "Give someone permission to be silly"

### 5.3 City sponsorships (careful)
- Local businesses can "sponsor" a city's bulletin board
- Not banner ads. More like: "This week's missions brought to you by [cool local bookshop]"
- Only businesses that match the vibe. No banks. No insurance companies.

### 5.4 NOT doing
- ❌ No data selling
- ❌ No targeted advertising
- ❌ No premium matching algorithms
- ❌ No "boost your profile" nonsense
- ❌ No subscription tiers that gate basic features
- ❌ No investor-pressure growth hacking

---

## PHASE 6 — Scale & Culture (Month 4+)
### Goal: Grow without losing the soul.

### 6.1 Mission creators
- Open mission creation to top community members
- "Sidekick Scribes" — people who write great missions
- Community-submitted missions go through curation
- Best ones get added to the main rotation with credit

### 6.2 Sidekick Chapters
- City-level communities with local leaders
- Chapter leaders organise pop-up sessions
- They get free kits and a tiny budget
- Organic, not corporate. More like a book club than a franchise.

### 6.3 The Sidekick Foundation
- When we're big enough: fund playfulness
- Grants for playgrounds, public art, community spaces
- "We made money from adult play. We're giving it back to actual play."

